WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.740
The first film followed additions and losses through one population window.

2
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.000
What pushes those arrows in the real Bay?

3
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.440
Keep that window open as cold, shelter, predators, and harvest change around it.

4
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:16.880
The same colour map stays.

5
00:00:20.383 --> 00:00:23.603
Scientists ask two separate questions about a factor.

6
00:00:24.823 --> 00:00:27.703
First, which living and nonliving parts are involved?

7
00:00:29.123 --> 00:00:32.663
Biotic factors are living parts, such as grass and big crabs.

8
00:00:34.103 --> 00:00:38.223
Abiotic factors are nonliving parts, such as temperature and salt.

9
00:00:39.583 --> 00:00:42.583
Second, is the change natural, human-caused, or both?

10
00:00:43.783 --> 00:00:46.283
A cold winter is abiotic and natural.

11
00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:49.943
A stone wall is abiotic and human-made.

12
00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.017
Watch a nonliving factor act.

13
00:00:54.277 --> 00:00:58.217
During a very cold winter, more buried crabs can die before spring.

14
00:00:59.797 --> 00:01:04.257
Lab tests also show especially low survival in cold, low-salt water.

15
00:01:05.637 --> 00:01:07.697
Both conditions can widen the death arrow.

16
00:01:08.937 --> 00:01:10.317
They may also act together.

17
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.640
Now watch living and nonliving parts work together.

18
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.160
Young crabs use grass and shallow water as refuge from bigger crabs.

19
00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.460
With less refuge, more young crabs may stay exposed.

20
00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.540
That can increase deaths from predation.

21
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.980
Refuge changes risk, not certainty.

22
00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:35.470
Suppose a stone wall replaces a gently sloping shore.

23
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.610
The shallow refuge becomes smaller.

24
00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:43.210
Which population arrow could change first, and in which direction?

25
00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.050
Think in arrows, not labels.

26
00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:55.893
The death arrow could widen if more exposed young crabs are eaten.

27
00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:59.873
The wall is not the only possible cause of change.

28
00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:06.073
It alters habitat, while cold, harvest, and other factors may change other arrows.

29
00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.073
That wording keeps the claim honest.

30
00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:12.273
Harvest is a human-caused loss.

31
00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:18.033
Overharvesting means removing a species faster than it can replace itself.

32
00:02:19.653 --> 00:02:22.033
Female crabs carry eggs for the next generation.

33
00:02:23.433 --> 00:02:27.813
Leaving more adults can support later births, but the other arrows keep moving.

34
00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:31.333
More adults do not guarantee more survivors.

35
00:02:32.533 --> 00:02:37.793
Sustainable harvest means taking only as many as the population can replace over

36
00:02:37.793 --> 00:02:43.633
time. A harvest limit can reduce one loss and leave more adults to reproduce.

37
00:02:45.073 --> 00:02:49.473
A harsh winter, poor refuge, or few new young can still slow recovery.

38
00:02:50.813 --> 00:02:52.353
So recovery is not certain.

39
00:02:53.733 --> 00:02:55.413
Managers keep measuring every year.

40
00:02:56.417 --> 00:03:00.757
A population graph shows what changed, not which factor caused it.

41
00:03:01.797 --> 00:03:05.477
To test a cause, compare the graph with measurements of that factor.

42
00:03:07.137 --> 00:03:10.417
Survey estimates, experiments, and models each add evidence.

43
00:03:11.877 --> 00:03:13.557
None makes every arrow stand still.

44
00:03:14.857 --> 00:03:17.097
Together, they narrow possible explanations.

45
00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:20.050
Return to the shared window.

46
00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:25.790
Natural events and human actions can change the same additions and losses.

47
00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:31.030
Management can change an arrow, but not command the whole population.

48
00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.870
The balance still decides the direction of change.
